# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Custom
.DS_Store

# Internal architecture notes (see concepts/README.md), anchored to the repository
# root.
#
# The third-party corpus — the TM Forum OpenAPI documents the coverage and
# server-conformance suites read — lives at `concepts/reference/` and is covered by
# this line. It is Apache-2.0 and public, so it is fetched rather than committed:
# `scripts/references.sh` pins every document to an upstream commit and a SHA-256,
# and `concepts/REFERENCES.md` is the index.
/concepts/

# This project's own feature specifications, and the Spec Kit machinery that produces
# them: `specs/NNN-slug/` (spec, plan, research, tasks), `.specify/memory/constitution.md`,
# and the `/speckit-*` skills. Same rule as `concepts/` — internal, and the published
# tree may not cite a path its reader does not have; scripts/concepts-check.sh fails on
# one that does. Matching billing, sepa and eebus.
#
# Until 2026-11-19 `specs/` held the OpenAPI documents now under `concepts/reference/oas/`.
/specs/
/.specify/
/.claude/
/.agents/skills/speckit-*/
